<p>You got across that he was being manipulated by his superiors. That's my problem.</p>
<p>Simply put, the priest's sudden mood swing seems completely insane from the perspective of someone who genuinely believes he has been asked to broker a deal. At the first slight hiccup in the plan (something which any sane individual might be able to predict, outside of the Foundation's lying ways), he decides everyone in the room has to die, ruining an agreement that could ensure lasting peace and progress between his own side and an extremely important and powerful potential ally. The sheer stupidity of that decision, and the bizarre mood swing involved, simply doesn't seem realistic to me, and as a result it sinks the log and the entire article in my eyes.</p>

